Medusa inspired the Greek myth of the Gorgon, a monster with snakes for hair which could turn its onlookers to stone. In the legends, there were three Gorgon sisters, with stories saying they shared a single eye between them. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}} Medusa's Amulet was eventually hidden away in a [[Medusa's Cave|cave]] on an isolated [[Medusa's Island|island]] in the [[Aegean Sea]], and was believed by many modern Seekers to be missing since the time of the ancient Greeks. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}

Many centuries later, Medusa's location was tracked down by [[the Organization]]. However, [[Wilder]] planned for his right-hand man, [[Stack]] to obtain the Amulet and offer it to the [[Blood Spiral]] in order to join and infiltrate the group for his own end. Although the Huntik Foundation team successfully intercepted and defeated Wilder's forces on the shores of the island, Stack and the ruthless Blood Spiral warrior [[Kiel]]  reached the cave first, and Stack invoked the cave's mechanism to call out Medusa. In an attempt to counter her Stonegaze ability, he invoked [[Divine Mirror Kagami]]. However, Medusa's raw aggression and volatile temperament proved far more difficult to subdue than he anticipated, rapidly breaking Kagami's mirror. At that moment, the Huntik team launched an offensive on Kiel and his forces. 

During the battle, [[Lok Lambert]], [[Zhalia Moon]], and [[Cherit]] worked to solve the cave's ancient puzzle of the Gorgon sisters. Zhalia informed Lok that the sculptures of the three creatures were Gorgon sisters who shared a single eye. Upon noticing that the light could travel between the stones in the Gorgons' eye sockets, Zhalia and Cherit directed the remaining stones at Lok, who ordered Medusa to return. Upon defeating Kagami, Medusa obeyed and returned to the stone, which shattered, revealing her Amulet, which Lok safely recovered.  {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}
